[{"id":36284,"sender_id":43,"sender_full_name":"DavidRoberts","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fbc2dbfb28f9e9275a4fd4cd109b5a21?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/16-Preprints-.26-Publications/topic/New.20paper.20about.20WISC.2C.20and.20the.20indepence.20thereof.20from.20ZF.20et.E2.80.A6/near/36284\">#1</a> I’d like to announce the arrival of the pre-preprint <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">¬</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{Con}(\\mathrm{ZF}+\\neg {\\mathrm{WISC}})</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Con</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">ZF</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">¬</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">WISC</span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>, available <a href=\"http://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/notWISC2.pdf\">here</a>. Abstract:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>By considering a variant on forcing using a symmetric model for a proper class-sized\n    group, we show that the very weak choice principle <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/WISC\">WISC</a>—the statement that there is at most a \n    set of incomparable surjections onto every set—is independent of the rest of the axioms \n    of set theory, in particular those of ZF. Our result applies to any set theory which gives rise to a \n    well-pointed boolean topos with nno. The proof does not rely on the axiom of choice, nor does it \n    make any large cardinal assumptions.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Comments and criticisms, please.</p>","timestamp":1352339588,"subject":"New paper about WISC, and the indepence thereof from ZF et…","stream_id":16,"display_recipient":"Preprints & Publications","reactions":[]},{"id":36432,"sender_id":14,"sender_full_name":"TobyBartels","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7ac66e2e51d2a389b2ab9b2a99100a0c?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/16-Preprints-.26-Publications/topic/New.20paper.20about.20WISC.2C.20and.20the.20indepence.20thereof.20from.20ZF.20et.E2.80.A6/near/36432\">#2</a> Maybe this is clear if I read the paper, but this doesn't sound right:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Our result applies to any set theory which gives rise to a well-pointed boolean topos with nno.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>Surely ZF + WISC is a set theory that gives rise to a well-pointed boolean topos with NNO, but WISC is not independent of ZF + WISC.</p>","timestamp":1352774054,"subject":"New paper about WISC, and the indepence thereof from ZF et…","stream_id":16,"display_recipient":"Preprints & Publications","reactions":[]},{"id":36433,"sender_id":14,"sender_full_name":"TobyBartels","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7ac66e2e51d2a389b2ab9b2a99100a0c?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/16-Preprints-.26-Publications/topic/New.20paper.20about.20WISC.2C.20and.20the.20indepence.20thereof.20from.20ZF.20et.E2.80.A6/near/36433\">#3</a> Well, looking at the first few pages, you seem to mean that given any well-pointed boolean topos <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span></span></span></span> with NNO, you construct a boolean <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span></span></span></span>-topos <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">E</span></span></span></span> in which WISC fails (and there's something about local connectedness in there too); but that doesn't mean that given a set theory <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span></span></span></span> and a (or the free?) model <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">S</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">S</span></span></span></span> of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span></span></span></span> that this <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">E</span></span></span></span> is a model of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">T</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.1389em;\">T</span></span></span></span>.  Whereas, presumably you do want that <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">E</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0576em;\">E</span></span></span></span> is a model of ZF.</p>\n<p>So rather than</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Our result applies to any set theory which gives rise to a well-pointed boolean topos with nno.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>it should be</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Our result applies to any well-pointed boolean topos with nno.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>(Or so it appears based on reading three pages!)</p>","timestamp":1352774514,"subject":"New paper about WISC, and the indepence thereof from ZF et…","stream_id":16,"display_recipient":"Preprints & Publications","reactions":[]},{"id":36434,"sender_id":43,"sender_full_name":"DavidRoberts","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fbc2dbfb28f9e9275a4fd4cd109b5a21?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/16-Preprints-.26-Publications/topic/New.20paper.20about.20WISC.2C.20and.20the.20indepence.20thereof.20from.20ZF.20et.E2.80.A6/near/36434\">#4</a> Ok, really it should mean something like ‘relatively consistent with’. My aim is to show that <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>⇒</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">¬</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{Con}(\\mathrm{ZF}) \\Rightarrow {\\mathrm{Con}}(\\mathrm{ZF} + \\neg {\\mathrm{WISC}})</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Con</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">ZF</span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">⇒</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Con</span></span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">ZF</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">¬</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">WISC</span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>, or possibly with <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{Con}(\\mathrm{ZFC})</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Con</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">ZFC</span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span> instead of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{Con}(\\mathrm{ZF})</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Con</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">ZF</span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>, but I think the LHS can be replaced with <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{Con}(\\mathrm{SEAR}[-C])</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Con</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">SEAR</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">[</span><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0715em;\">C</span><span class=\"mclose\">])</span></span></span></span> with the result being <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">¬</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{Con}(\\mathrm{SEAR} + \\neg {\\mathrm{WISC}})</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">Con</span></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">SEAR</span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">¬</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">WISC</span></span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span></span></span></span>, and ditto for <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{ETCS}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">ETCS</span></span></span></span></span> (by the way, what do people call <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{ETCS}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">ETCS</span></span></span></span></span> without AC?)</p>\n<p>In fact (thanks to comments from Mike) I know I haven’t quite got the material set theory version yet, but I think the structural version is complete (I haven’t got the structural<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>→</mo></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\to</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.3669em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">→</span></span></span></span>material translation done).</p>\n<p>So your last comment is correct.</p>","timestamp":1352774755,"subject":"New paper about WISC, and the indepence thereof from ZF et…","stream_id":16,"display_recipient":"Preprints & Publications","reactions":[]},{"id":36439,"sender_id":14,"sender_full_name":"TobyBartels","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7ac66e2e51d2a389b2ab9b2a99100a0c?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/16-Preprints-.26-Publications/topic/New.20paper.20about.20WISC.2C.20and.20the.20indepence.20thereof.20from.20ZF.20et.E2.80.A6/near/36439\">#5</a> [never mind]</p>","timestamp":1352776786,"subject":"New paper about WISC, and the indepence thereof from ZF et…","stream_id":16,"display_recipient":"Preprints & Publications","reactions":[]},{"id":36440,"sender_id":14,"sender_full_name":"TobyBartels","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/7ac66e2e51d2a389b2ab9b2a99100a0c?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/16-Preprints-.26-Publications/topic/New.20paper.20about.20WISC.2C.20and.20the.20indepence.20thereof.20from.20ZF.20et.E2.80.A6/near/36440\">#6</a></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>by the way, what do people call <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{ETCS}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">ETCS</span></span></span></span></span> without AC?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>There's <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{CETCS}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">CETCS</span></span></span></span></span> (constructive ETCS), but that's missing more.  Maybe ‘<span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{ETS}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">ETS</span></span></span></span></span>’ (^_^)?</p>","timestamp":1352776841,"subject":"New paper about WISC, and the indepence thereof from ZF et…","stream_id":16,"display_recipient":"Preprints & Publications","reactions":[]},{"id":36441,"sender_id":43,"sender_full_name":"DavidRoberts","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fbc2dbfb28f9e9275a4fd4cd109b5a21?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/16-Preprints-.26-Publications/topic/New.20paper.20about.20WISC.2C.20and.20the.20indepence.20thereof.20from.20ZF.20et.E2.80.A6/near/36441\">#7</a></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>There’s CETCS (constructive ETCS), but that’s missing more.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I definitely need classical logic for the current proof to work…</p>","timestamp":1352777121,"subject":"New paper about WISC, and the indepence thereof from ZF et…","stream_id":16,"display_recipient":"Preprints & Publications","reactions":[]},{"id":36508,"sender_id":43,"sender_full_name":"DavidRoberts","avatar_url":"https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fbc2dbfb28f9e9275a4fd4cd109b5a21?d=identicon&version=1","content":"<p><a href=\"#narrow/channel/16-Preprints-.26-Publications/topic/New.20paper.20about.20WISC.2C.20and.20the.20indepence.20thereof.20from.20ZF.20et.E2.80.A6/near/36508\">#8</a> After Mike’s comments alluded to above, I have resurrected the following material set theory version:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>If ZF is consistent, then so is <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/ZFA\">ZFA</a><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∃</mi><mtext> a proper class of atoms</mtext><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">¬</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\"> + (\\exists \\text{ a proper class of atoms}) + \\neg {\\mathrm{WISC}}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">+</span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord\">∃</span><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\"> a proper class of atoms</span></span><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">+</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\">¬</span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">WISC</span></span></span></span></span></span></p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I’m still working on the independence from <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Z</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\mathrm{ZF}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6833em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathrm\">ZF</span></span></span></span></span>.</p>\n<p>So as it stands, I have only given a pre-Cohen-style independence result, but as a corollary, I now understand the so-called Fraenkel model: it is the material set theory arising from the topos of sets with an action of an open subgroup of <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">Z</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mn>2</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">N</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(\\mathbb{Z}/2)^\\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0952em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathbb\">Z</span><span class=\"mord\">/2</span><span class=\"mclose\"><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8452em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathbb mtight\">N</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> for a certain natural topology on this group. Open subgroups are the finite-index subgroups <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>×</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">Z</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mn>2</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">N</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">\\prod_{i\\in I} H_i\\times (\\mathbb{Z}/2)^{\\mathbb{N} - I}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0771em;vertical-align:-0.3271em;\"></span><span class=\"mop\"><span class=\"mop op-symbol small-op\" style=\"position:relative;top:0em;\">∏</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.1786em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.4003em;margin-left:0em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span><span class=\"mrel mtight\">∈</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">I</span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3271em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.1667em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0813em;\">H</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0813em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span><span class=\"mbin\">×</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2222em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1.0952em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mopen\">(</span><span class=\"mord mathbb\">Z</span><span class=\"mord\">/2</span><span class=\"mclose\"><span class=\"mclose\">)</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.8452em;\"><span style=\"top:-3.063em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathbb mtight\">N</span><span class=\"mbin mtight\">−</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">I</span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span></span> for finite <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">N</mi></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">I\\subset \\mathbb{N}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.7224em;vertical-align:-0.0391em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0785em;\">I</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">⊂</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.6889em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbb\">N</span></span></span></span> and <span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-mathml\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant=\"double-struck\">Z</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">/</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">H_i \\le \\mathbb{Z}/2</annotation></semantics></math></span><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:0.8333em;vertical-align:-0.15em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.0813em;\">H</span><span class=\"msupsub\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.3117em;\"><span style=\"top:-2.55em;margin-left:-0.0813em;margin-right:0.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:2.7em;\"></span><span class=\"sizing reset-size6 size3 mtight\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal mtight\">i</span></span></span></span><span class=\"vlist-s\">​</span></span><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.15em;\"><span></span></span></span></span></span></span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span><span class=\"mrel\">≤</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-right:0.2778em;\"></span></span><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:1em;vertical-align:-0.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mord mathbb\">Z</span><span class=\"mord\">/2</span></span></span></span>. Arrows in this topos are allowed to be equivariant for an open (possibly proper) subgroup of the groups acting on the domain and codomain.</p>\n<p>I have put the above description at <a href=\"https://ncatlab.org/nlab/show/Fraenkel%20model%20of%20ZFA\">Fraenkel model of ZFA</a>.</p>","timestamp":1353049925,"subject":"New paper about WISC, and the indepence thereof from ZF et…","stream_id":16,"display_recipient":"Preprints & Publications","reactions":[]}]